<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raymond Bernard Trencavel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1074</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raymond Bernard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-trencavel">Trencavel</a> was viscount of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albi">Albi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nimes">Nîmes</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a> in the 11th century, whose nickname Trencavel was later adopted as the name of his dynasty. Around 1067 he acquired rights over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carcassonne">Carcassonne</a> through his wife Ermengard, heiress of the counts of Carcassonne, laying the foundation of the Trencavel principality ruled by their son Bernard Ato IV.</p></div>
